  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Effective social dialogue and tripartite processes at the different levels toward better-informed and consensus-driven policies and decisions on social and economic matters</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PHL 129 strengthens social dialogue and tripartite processes at national, regional, sectoral and workplace levels to support evidence-based, consensus-driven policies and decisions on labour, social, and economic matters. It aligns with the Labour and Employment Plan (LEP) 2023&#x2013;2028&#x2019;s priority on labour market governance and contributes to the UN Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework (UN SDCF) 2024&#x2013;2028&#x2019;s strategic priority on sustainable economic development and decent work. The initiative reinforces institutions that foster inclusive, rights-based workplace practices and policies.

PHL 129 benefits workers&#x2019; and employers&#x2019; representative organizations, as well as government institutions with a mandate to regulate labour markets. Its interventions strengthen the capacity of labour administration authorities to enforce labour standards and eliminate unacceptable forms of work, while equipping workers&#x2019; and employers&#x2019; organizations to address labour market challenges through social dialogue and sound industrial relations. The initiatives modernize policy, legal, and institutional frameworks for labour protection; strengthens dispute resolution and case management systems; reinforces bipartite workplace cooperation mechanisms at the enterprise level; and supports the establishment and operationalization of National, Regional, and Industry Tripartite Councils.

Implemented in collaboration with government institutions, employers&#x2019; and workers&#x2019; organizations, its strategy strengthens tripartism, improves policy coherence, and reinforces accountability and trust on labour governance mechanism. By addressing structural gaps in labour governance and empowering tripartite partners, PHL 129 contributes to more transparent, democratic, inclusive, and rights-based labour market systems.</narrative>
  </description>
